    { number := 159, text := "" },
    { number := 160, text := "### 3.22 Named hole" },
    { number := 161, text := "" },
    { number := 162, text := "An explicit, tracked absence of a target WordID when emit cannot find an accepted Rosetta relation for a source WordID under the target LanguageID." },
    { number := 163, text := "" },
    { number := 164, text := "## 4. Core requirements" },
    { number := 165, text := "" },
    { number := 166, text := "### 4.1 Representation" },
    { number := 167, text := "" },
    { number := 168, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MUST encode programs as language runs (Clause 3.2)." },
    { number := 169, text := "2. In a serialized stream of language runs, a LanguageID prefix MUST appear when the language of the following WordID sequence differs from the previous language in that stream, including at the start of the stream. A LanguageID prefix MUST NOT be repeated before every WordID when the language has not changed." },
    { number := 170, text := "3. LanguageID values MUST be 64 bit sequential integers (Clause 3.3)." },
    { number := 171, text := "4. WordID values MUST be 64 bit sequential integers assigned per LanguageID (Clause 3.4)." },
    { number := 172, text := "5. Hashing MUST NOT be primary identity for languages or words (Clause 3.5). A digest of surface text MAY exist as an auxiliary index. An auxiliary index MUST NOT replace sequential LanguageID or sequential WordID as the stored identifier used for lookup, persistence, or Rosetta relations." },
    { number := 173, text := "6. Combined identifier capacity MUST be `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs." },
    { number := 174, text := "7. Items 1 through 6 are requirements. This document does not claim an encoder, a vocabulary store, or sequential WordID assignment is implemented." },
    { number := 175, text := "" },
    { number := 176, text := "### 4.2 Rosetta" },
    { number := 177, text := "" },
    { number := 178, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MUST represent each accepted cross language correspondence as a Rosetta relation (Clause 3.7) with fields LanguageID of language A, WordID in language A, RelationType, LanguageID of language B, WordID in language B, and Provenance." },
    { number := 179, text := "2. Provenance MUST be `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven` (Clause 3.9)." },
    { number := 180, text := "3. A RelationType MUST be present (Clause 3.8)." },
    { number := 181, text := "4. Rosetta relations MUST use sequential LanguageID and WordID values. They MUST NOT use hashing as primary identity of either endpoint." },
    { number := 182, text := "5. Items 1 through 4 are requirements. This document does not claim a Rosetta store is implemented." },
    { number := 183, text := "" },
    { number := 184, text := "### 4.3 Pipeline" },
    { number := 185, text := "" },
    { number := 186, text := "1. Given the same vocabulary and the same set of accepted Rosetta relations, the pipeline MUST be deterministic: the same source token sequence and the same target LanguageID MUST produce the same emit." },
    { number := 187, text := "2. The pipeline MUST ingest source text and tokenize it into candidate surface tokens." },
    { number := 188, text := "3. The pipeline MUST look up each token in the vocabulary for the current LanguageID, or insert a new sequential WordID when the token is new in that language." },
    { number := 189, text := "4. The intermediate representation MUST be language runs plus accepted Rosetta relations (Clause 3.11)." },
    { number := 190, text := "5. The pipeline MAY formalize fragments of that intermediate representation into Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
    { number := 191, text := "6. Emit MUST map source WordID values to target WordID values by inverse lookup under the target LanguageID through accepted Rosetta relations." },
    { number := 192, text := "7. If no accepted Rosetta relation provides a target WordID, a conforming implementation MUST NOT invent hashing as the identity of that token. It MUST either fail the translation of that token or emit a named hole (Clause 3.22). Choosing between those two outcomes is defined by the implementation." },
    { number := 193, text := "8. Items 1 through 4, 6, and 7 are requirements. Item 5 is optional. This document does not claim a pipeline is implemented." },
    { number := 194, text := "" },
    { number := 195, text := "### 4.4 Neural proposals" },
    { number := 196, text := "" },
    { number := 197, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MAY accept neural proposals (Clause 3.12)." },
    { number := 198, text := "2. A neural proposal MUST be reduced to sequential integers (LanguageID, WordID, and any other integers this specification uses as identity) before it is accepted into the vocabulary or the Rosetta relation set." },
    { number := 199, text := "3. A neural proposal that has not been reduced to sequential integers MUST NOT be accepted." },
    { number := 200, text := "4. When a neural proposal would become authoritative for semantics or for behavior that is safety critical, it SHOULD be Lean proven before it is treated as authoritative. That SHOULD is not a substitute for item 2." },
    { number := 201, text := "5. Items 2 and 3 are requirements. Item 1 is optional. Item 4 is a SHOULD. This document does not claim a neural proposer exists." },
    { number := 202, text := "" },
    { number := 203, text := "### 4.5 Natural language translation" },
    { number := 204, text := "" },
    { number := 205, text := "1. A conforming SSSSS MAY offer written natural language translation (Clause 3.13)." },
    { number := 206, text := "2. Natural language translation is best effort and is not required to be deterministic in the sense of Clause 4.3 item 1." },
    { number := 207, text := "3. A natural language translation MUST be marked provisional unless it is Lean proven or it carries a high confidence mark (Clause 3.14)." },
    { number := 208, text := "4. Best effort natural language translation MUST NOT be treated as a substitute for deterministic programming language translation (Clause 4.3)." },
    { number := 209, text := "5. Items 3 and 4 are requirements when natural language translation is offered. Item 1 is optional. This document does not claim a natural language translator exists." },
    { number := 210, text := "" },
    { number := 211, text := "### 4.6 Durable state, Systems Lean core, and 0002 validation" },
    { number := 212, text := "" },
    { number := 213, text := "1. Durable SSSSS state MUST be stored in beastdb as specified in [0003_beastdb.md](0003_beastdb.md)." },
    { number := 214, text := "2. The core of SSSSS MUST be implemented in Systems Lean as specified in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md)." },
    { number := 215, text := "3. SSSSS components that are safety critical, SSSSS components that run in environments with tight resources, and SSSSS components that are freestanding MUST be able to target the freestanding Slake path in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md). Those components MUST contain no managed Lean runtime and MUST NOT perform garbage collection on the freestanding product wire." },
    { number := 216, text := "4. CompCert verified compilation (Clause 3.20) is a REQUIRED core validation step for the freestanding C emit of the components named in item 3, as required by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.2 item 6. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. This document does not claim CompCert is pinned under this specifications repository's `ref/`." },
    { number := 217, text := "5. Bootstrapping a Slake compiler that fully typechecks (Clause 3.21) is a REQUIRED core validation step for those same components, as required by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) Clause 4.2 item 7. A named subset of modules is not enough. Naming a residual MUST NOT substitute for this step. A claim that the freestanding product hosts itself from generated C is a distinct claim and does not satisfy this step by itself." },
    { number := 218, text := "6. Residual honesty as defined in [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) remains required for the freestanding product wire. Residual honesty MUST NOT replace items 4 and 5." },
    { number := 219, text := "7. Items 1 through 6 are requirements. This document does not claim an SSSSS backed by beastdb, an SSSSS core built by Slake, CompCert validation of an SSSSS emit, or a Slake bootstrap that fully typechecks for SSSSS is implemented." },
    { number := 220, text := "" },
    { number := 221, text := "## 5. Conformance" },
    { number := 222, text := "" },
    { number := 223, text := "An SSSSS implementation conforms to this specification if and only if all of the following hold:" },
    { number := 224, text := "" },
    { number := 225, text := "1. It encodes programs as language runs, emits a LanguageID prefix only when the language changes (including at stream start), uses 64 bit sequential LanguageID and per language sequential WordID values, does not use hashing as primary identity, and provides combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs (Clause 4.1)." },
    { number := 226, text := "2. It represents accepted cross language correspondences as Rosetta relations with RelationType and provenance `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven`, using sequential LanguageID and WordID at both endpoints (Clause 4.2)." },
    { number := 227, text := "3. Given the same vocabulary and the same accepted Rosetta relation set, its pipeline is deterministic; it ingests and tokenizes, looks up or inserts sequential WordIDs, uses language runs plus Rosetta relations as intermediate representation, emits by inverse WordID lookup under the target LanguageID, and on a missing mapping fails that token or emits a named hole without inventing hash identity (Clause 4.3 items 1 through 4, 6, and 7). Formalizing fragments into Systems Lean (Clause 4.3 item 5) is not required." },
    { number := 228, text := "4. Every accepted neural proposal has been reduced to sequential integers (Clause 4.4 items 2 and 3). When natural language translation is offered, each such translation is marked provisional unless it is Lean proven or carries a high confidence mark, and natural language translation is not treated as a substitute for deterministic programming language translation (Clause 4.5). Neural proposals and natural language translation MAY be absent." },
    { number := 229, text := "5. Durable state is stored in beastdb (Clause 4.6 item 1). The core is implemented in Systems Lean (Clause 4.6 item 2). SSSSS components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding target the freestanding Slake path without managed Lean runtime or garbage collection, CompCert verified compilation of their freestanding C emit has been performed, and a bootstrapped Slake fully typechecks the Systems Lean and Slake sources it is bootstrapped from (Clause 4.6 items 3 through 6). A named residual MUST NOT substitute for CompCert verified compilation or for the bootstrap typecheck." },
    { number := 230, text := "" },
    { number := 231, text := "The cultural marker in Clause 1.3 is not a conformance item." },
    { number := 232, text := "" },
    { number := 233, text := "Optional neural proposals (Clause 4.4 item 1), optional Systems Lean formalization of fragments (Clause 4.3 item 5), and optional natural language translation (Clause 4.5 item 1) are not required for conformance when absent. When they are present, the MUST clauses that apply to them in Clause 5 items 3 and 4 still hold." },
    { number := 234, text := "" },
    { number := 235, text := "This specification is not itself a conforming implementation. Meeting these items is a claim about a product, not about this markdown file." },
    { number := 236, text := "" },
    { number := 237, text := "## 6. Residual" },
    { number := 238, text := "" },
    { number := 239, text := "This section is normative for residual honesty of this document. It does not add product behavior beyond Clauses 4 and 5. Silence about an unpublished specification, an unassigned number, an unnumbered substrate, an unimplemented requirement, or an optional path named in this document is nonconforming for this specification as a document. A parenthetical planned file name in Scope is not the residual record. The repository root `RESIDUAL.md` restates residual for the numbered specification program; this clause is the residual record for this specification." },
    { number := 240, text := "" },
    { number := 241, text := "### 6.1 Unpublished specifications and unassigned numbers" },
    { number := 242, text := "" },
    { number := 243, text := "1. fargo has no assigned specification number. A previous plan that assigned number 0005 to fargo is withdrawn. Number 0005 is Concise American Technical English (`0005_CATE.md`). Number 0006 is Recursive Self Improvement (`0006_RSI.md`). This document does not invent a new number for fargo. This document does not require fargo." },
    { number := 244, text := "2. The Carbonado Network Protocol is deferred. It has no numbered specification file in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. Discussion has mentioned 0006 as a possible later number. That mention is not an assignment. This document does not create a file for it." },
    { number := 245, text := "" },
    { number := 246, text := "### 6.2 Lean Machine unnumbered" },
    { number := 247, text := "" },
    { number := 248, text := "1. Lean Machine is named in Scope as a substrate. It has no numbered specification in this repository. It has no assigned specification number. This document MUST NOT be read as creating a numbered specification for Lean Machine or as assigning it a number." },
    { number := 249, text := "" },
    { number := 250, text := "### 6.3 Product tree pins versus this repository's `ref/`" },
    { number := 251, text := "" },
    { number := 252, text := "1. `0000_spec.md` Clause 12 binds external specifications this specifications repository cites to `ref/` in this repository." },
    { number := 253, text := "2. Lean 4, Idris 2, CompCert, and Rust are cited by [0002_Systems_Lean.md](0002_Systems_Lean.md) as Form 1 pins of the Systems Lean product tree, not of this specifications repository's `ref/`. This document does not move those pins here." },
    { number := 254, text := "3. There is no SSSSS product tree pin in this repository. SSSSS work is ongoing and is not ready for use. This document MUST NOT be read as claiming that SSSSS never started or does not exist." },
    { number := 255, text := "4. beastdb is specified in this repository as `0003_beastdb.md`. That numbered specification is not a `ref/` pin of an upstream store." },
    { number := 256, text := "" },
    { number := 257, text := "### 6.4 Product requirements that are not ready for use" },
    { number := 258, text := "" },
    { number := 259, text := "This document specifies SSSSS. The work is ongoing and is not ready for use. It MUST NOT be read as claiming that SSSSS never started or does not exist. The following are requirements in Clause 4, not done work:" },
    { number := 260, text := "" },
    { number := 261, text := "1. Encoding as sequential language runs with LanguageID prefix only on change." },
    { number := 262, text := "2. Sequential LanguageID and sequential WordID as primary identity, including the hashing ban as a requirement (not as proof that an engine already obeys it)." },
    { number := 263, text := "3. Combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs." },
    { number := 264, text := "4. Rosetta relations with RelationType and provenance tags." },
    { number := 265, text := "5. A deterministic pipeline given the same vocabulary and relation set, including ingest, tokenize, vocabulary lookup or insert, intermediate representation, and emit by inverse lookup." },
    { number := 266, text := "6. Failure or a named hole when no accepted mapping exists, without inventing hash identity." },
    { number := 267, text := "7. Reduction of any accepted neural proposal to sequential integers." },
    { number := 268, text := "8. Provisional marking of natural language translation unless Lean proven or high confidence." },
    { number := 269, text := "9. Durable state in beastdb." },
    { number := 270, text := "10. A Systems Lean core that can target the freestanding Slake path for components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding, with CompCert verified compilation and a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks as required by Clause 4.6. Residual honesty does not substitute for those validation steps." },
    { number := 271, text := "" },
    { number := 272, text := "### 6.5 Informative and optional items this document names" },
    { number := 273, text := "" },
    { number := 274, text := "1. The Rick and Morty cultural marker (Clause 1.3) is informative. Television canon is not a conformance item." },
    { number := 275, text := "2. Neural proposals are MAY (Clause 4.4). Lean proving a neural proposal before it becomes authoritative for semantics or behavior that is safety critical is SHOULD, not MUST." },
    { number := 276, text := "3. Natural language translation is MAY, best effort, and provisional unless proven or high confidence (Clause 4.5)." },
    { number := 277, text := "4. Formalizing fragments into Systems Lean is MAY (Clause 4.3 item 5)." },
    { number := 278, text := "5. An auxiliary hash index is allowed only as an index that is not primary (Clause 4.1 item 5)." },
    { number := 279, text := "" },
    { number := 280, text := "## 7. Changelog" },
    { number := 281, text := "" },
    { number := 282, text := "### 1.0.0 - 20260824" },
    { number := 283, text := "" },
    { number := 284, text := "First publication of this specification text. Defines SSSSS as specification 0004 with file name `0004_SSSSS.md`; requires sequential language runs with LanguageID prefix only on change; requires 64 bit sequential LanguageID and per language sequential WordID as primary identity and forbids hashing as primary identity; states combined capacity `2^64` languages times `2^64` WordIDs; requires Rosetta relations with RelationType and provenance `neural-proposed`, `human-confirmed`, or `Lean-proven`; requires a deterministic pipeline given the same vocabulary and relation set; permits neural proposals only after reduction to sequential integers; permits natural language translation as best effort work that MUST be marked provisional unless Lean proven or high confidence; requires durable state in beastdb as specified in `0003_beastdb.md`; requires a Systems Lean core as specified in `0002_Systems_Lean.md`; and requires CompCert verified compilation and a bootstrapped Slake that fully typechecks for SSSSS components that are safety critical, that run in environments with tight resources, and that are freestanding, with residual honesty not substituting for those steps." },
    { number := 285, text := "" },
    { number := 286, text := "This 1.0.0 also records: this document does not claim a conforming implementation exists; Lean Machine has no numbered specification; fargo has no assigned specification number and is not required here; Recursive Self Improvement is specified in `0006_RSI.md`; the Carbonado Network Protocol has no assigned number; the five consecutive S letters are an informative cultural marker and not a conformance item." },
    { number := 287, text := "" },
    { number := 288, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that hyphenated modifiers in prose were rephrased into ordinary English. Deleting the hyphen and leaving the same two words is not enough." },
    { number := 289, text := "" },
    { number := 290, text := "This unpublished 1.0.0 also records that citations of Keagan McLelland (Proof of Keags) research SHALL keep the publisher links on those pages (back linking)." },
    { number := 291, text := "" },
